================================================================================

The blank outline is a variable-sided polygon. Edge count depends on flange config.

CORNER TYPE DEFINITIONS (current code):
  Type A (J+J): 4 edges — void_edge + miter + miter + void_edge
  Type B (any active corner without J+J): void edges to HC on cut when notch_size=0
          Covers L+L, J+L, and L+J. A J flange only receives a miter when it
          meets another J flange at the same corner.
  Type C (active+inactive): 1 edge  — square flange end
  Type D (inactive+inactive): 0 edges — face corner only

EDGE COUNTS BY FLANGE CODE:
  Config        | Corner Type | Corner Edges | Primary Edges | Total
  --------------|-------------|--------------|---------------|------
  J4S           | A×4         | 16           | 4             | 20
  L4S           | B×4         | 8            | 4             | 12
  J2TB          | C×4         | 4            | 4             | 8
  L2TB          | C×4         | 4            | 4             | 8
  J2LR          | C×4         | 4            | 4             | 8
  L2LR          | C×4         | 4            | 4             | 8
  MIX J-tb/L-lr | B×4         | 8            | 4             | 12

  NOTE — current DXF blank outline (cut layer):
    generate_panel_dxf passes notch_size = 0: no 2×T bend-1 intersection notch and
    no J+J five-point square detour on the cut polyline. Corners use void edges +
    miters (J+J) or straight segments to HC (non–J+J). Vertex count is closer to the
    abstract edge-count model than when relief notches were embedded. J4S miter/void
    dimensions (Fusion) for blank layout are unchanged.

VOID EDGE LENGTH RULE (perimeter `cut`; CI = SHOP_FLANGE_CORNER_INSET):
  J side at J+J corner:
    void_edge_length = f1 + CI
    This ensures the miter starts exactly at the bend2 centerline.

  Any side without a miter at that corner:
    void_edge_length = f1 + f2 + CI
    The path runs straight to the blank edge (square end).

J4S 20-POINT OUTLINE (blank coords, CCW):
   1: (fx0-vl,  fy0)       BL close miter end / left primary end
   2: (fx0,     fy0)       BL hard corner (void inner)
   3: (fx0,     fy0-vb)    BL void edge down
   4: (fx0+mb,  0)         BL miter end → bottom primary start
   5: (fx1-mb,  0)         bottom primary end
   6: (fx1,     fy0-vb)    BR miter end
   7: (fx1,     fy0)       BR hard corner
   8: (fx1+vr,  fy0)       BR void edge right
   9: (bw,      fy0+mr)    BR miter end → right primary start
  10: (bw,      fy1-mr)    right primary end
  11: (fx1+vr,  fy1)       TR miter end
  12: (fx1,     fy1)       TR hard corner
  13: (fx1,     fy1+vt)    TR void edge up
  14: (fx1-mt,  bh)        TR miter end → top primary start
  15: (fx0+mt,  bh)        top primary end
  16: (fx0,     fy1+vt)    TL miter end
  17: (fx0,     fy1)       TL hard corner
  18: (fx0-vl,  fy1)       TL void edge left
  19: (0,       fy1-ml)    TL miter end → left primary start
  20: (0,       fy0+ml)    left primary end

Where (ortho `cut` layer):
  fx0 = el+CI, fy0 = eb+CI   (BL void inner hard corner)
  fx1 = bw-er-CI, fy1 = bh-et-CI   (TR void inner hard corner)
  vb/vt/vl/vr = f1+CI (void edge lengths per side in the abstract model)
  mb/mt/ml/mr = f2 (miter depths per side, 0 for L flanges)

MITER GEOMETRY:
  Applied ONLY at J+J corners
  Nominal miter length = √2 × f2 = √2 × 2.084 = 2.948" ≈ shop 2.907" ✓
  Nominal miter angle  = 45°
  Miter starts at bend2 centerline level (not at blank edge)
  Miter ends on blank outer edge
  Purpose: allows flange2 (lip) to fold back without adjacent lips colliding
  gap_override (optional): opens the J+J miter apex by shifting the two
    void endpoints away from the hard corner by gap/2 each
  Default code behavior: gap = 0.0; back J-relief circle provides the relief


