SECTION 7 — FLANGE TYPES AND CODES
================================================================================

FLANGE CODES:
  L4S   — L flange all 4 sides, same depth
  J4S   — J flange all 4 sides, same depth
  L2TB  — L flange top + bottom only
  J2TB  — J flange top + bottom only
  L2LR  — L flange left + right only
  J2LR  — J flange left + right only
  MIX   — per-side type and depth via CSV columns

Single letters L and J are normalized to L4S and J4S.

J FLANGE PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION:
  Face flat → flange1 (leg) folds 90° AWAY from face → flange2 (lip) folds 90° BACK toward face
  Creates a J-channel profile when viewed in cross-section
  Target depth (face outside to inside face): flange1_depth (e.g., 2.0")
  Target lip width: flange2_depth (e.g., 2.25")
  Bend 1 = leg fold (tight to face), Bend 2 = lip return (the J return)

L FLANGE PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION:
  Face flat → flange1 (leg) folds 90° away from face
  Single bend, creates L-angle profile
  No lip return, no second bend

CORNER GEOMETRY BY FLANGE COMBINATION:
  J+J corner: void edges + miters on both flange ends
    Miter prevents adjacent lips from colliding when J returns fold back
  L+L corner: no miter; void edges to HC on cut outline (no embedded 2×T bend-relief square in DXF when notch_size=0)
  J+L or L+J corner: no miter; both sides terminate square at the corner
    The J flange is treated like an L at that corner because there is no
    opposing J return to collide with
  Active+Inactive: square end (flange just terminates at face edge)


