    face for void corners, so HC-HC on the cut outline is wider than the Fusion bend-
    deduction row by 2×(BD−CI) when CI < BD (by design for shop perimeter).
  ~ bend2 CL from HC: code=1.834" vs shop=1.815-1.823" (0.011-0.019" = rounding)
  ~ miter vertex X: code=1.834" vs shop=1.815" (0.019" = rounding)
  ~ miter angle stays exactly 45° only when gap_override = 0;
    if gap_override > 0 the apex opens slightly by design

CURRENT CODE STATUS:
  1. Material lookup table implemented
     - 3003, 5052, 6061, and steel all supported in MATERIAL_TABLE
     - nearest-thickness fallback still applies when no exact row exists

  2. Perimeter blank outline (cut layer): notch_size = 0 — no 2×T corner notch,
     no J+J five-point square on polyline; void + miter paths only.

  3. Bend centerlines on `bend` layer: L and J bend1; J bend2 when f2>0.
     L vs J bend1 offsets differ (_bend1_cl_positions, _draw_bend_lines, RT variant).

  4. Install slots (`fastening` layer)
     - L: 2" end margins, ~12" o.c., never above 13" between centers (`_l_positions`).
     - J return lip: shop offset uses **nominal** lip depth from CSV (`flange2_depth` or
       MIX `*_f2`): (slot center to blank **outer** lip, OC) = nominal_F2 − (hole center
       to inner **finished_face** edge, OC). Stations are taken only from the **outermost**
       perforation row or column toward that flange (stagger-safe); along-flange spacing
       is never greater than 12" c–c (tighter when the grid requires). J+J miters: along-
       flange coordinates trim by developed `f2` from each affected corner so slots stay
       in material outside the 45° miter. RT J slots use the same nominal-F2 rule with the
       finished-face edge sampled at each hole (`_j_slot_normal_rt`).
     - DXF plan view is **inside face up**; panel ID stick text is placed for that view
       (etch on an L leg can be hidden after forming when that leg folds outward).

  5. Panel ID (text layer)
     - Stick-font LWPOLYLINEs (no DXF TEXT / external fonts)
     - If the chosen ID flange is also in fastening_pair: anchor clears the
       first slot (≥4" from flange start from fx0/fy0, and past first slot center
       + half slot length + small gap); else mid-flange.

  6. L flat leg f1_flat = F1 - OSS + BA in code (matches §8 L_total); DXF bend-1
     CL differs by flange type (J: HC ± BA/2 from face+BD quad; L: `_f1_bend_inset_from_face`
     + BA/2). `cut` void HC uses CI from nominal face, not BD.

  7. Origin convention difference (documentation only)
     Known Truths: 0,0 at face corner
     Our DXF: 0,0 at blank corner (flanges extend inward)
     Both are correct — just different reference frames

REMAINING ENGINEERING GAPS:
  1. Nesting remains unimplemented (stub functions only)
  2. Install slot sizing now supports explicit slot_length in CSV; if left blank
     the default remains fastener_dia + 0.50"
  3. J install-slot rules (nominal F2 offset, outer perf line, ≤12" o.c., J+J trim) are
     implemented in `screenwall_generator.py`; further edge cases (very coarse pitch,
     margins vs slots) remain optional.

CONFLICTS (requires resolution):
  None confirmed. All apparent formula conflicts resolve to different reference
