SECTION 12 — CSV INPUT FORMAT
================================================================================

REQUIRED COLUMNS:
  panel_id, width, height, thickness, flange_code, flange1_depth,
  hole_diameter, hole_pitch, pattern, fastening_pair

OPTIONAL COLUMNS:
  flange2_depth, fastener_dia, slot_length, alloy, material,
  k_factor_override, bend_radius_override, gap_override,
  stagger_angle, margin

REQUIRED USER-CHOICE FIELD:
  fastening_pair
    Use tb / lr / t / b / l / r / none to explicitly choose which flanges
    receive install slots. Typical practice is the long sides only.
    Legacy all / standard values may still appear in older files.

MIX COLUMNS (required when flange_code=MIX):
  top_type, top_f1, top_f2
  bottom_type, bottom_f1, bottom_f2
  left_type, left_f1, left_f2
  right_type, right_f1, right_f2

THICKNESS INPUT:
  Accepts decimal inches:
    steel examples: 0.060, 0.075, 0.120, 0.250
    aluminum examples: 0.0625, 0.080, 0.125, 0.1875, 0.250
  Accepts gauge strings: "16 ga", "14 ga", "11 ga"
    material/alloy containing "steel" → 0.060 / 0.075 / 0.120
    otherwise → 0.0625 / 0.080 / 0.125

PATTERN VALUES: "straight" or "staggered"
FASTENING_PAIR VALUES: tb, lr, t, b, l, r, none
  Legacy values: all, standard
FASTENER_DIA:
  Width of the install slot
  Current code slot length = fastener_dia + 0.50"
  Accepted import aliases: slot_width, fastener_slot_width, install_slot_width
SLOT_LENGTH:
  Optional total install slot length
  Must be >= fastener_dia
  Leave blank to use the default: fastener_dia + 0.50"
  Accepted import aliases: fastener_slot_length, install_slot_length
FLANGE_CODE VALUES: L4S, J4S, L2TB, J2TB, L2LR, J2LR, MIX
  (single "L" or "J" normalized to L4S / J4S)


